{"authored" [{"question" "q-103770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/assets/749bafb0b977dc67bbf444edc6c51c884a55874655553671330462037c7f1e45.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. It consists of two lines and the arc of a quarter-circle of radius $2.$ Given $g(t)={\\int }_{-1}^{t}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x,$ determine the value of $g(3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Evaluating $g(t)$ at $t=3,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\ng(3)={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThis integral gives the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/assets/813a6e18ee953306699ffe65b5af99c9d44baa1d9e958572a6aad14b4e139f2c.png)\n\nNote that the graph above consists of $2$ parts:\n\n- $x\\in [-1,1],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a trapezoid. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{1}.$\n\n- $x\\in [1,3],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a quarter-circle cut out of a square. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\ng(3)={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute these integrals:\n\n- To find the first integral where $x\\in [-1,1],$ we compute the area ${A}_{1}$ of the trapezoid as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}h(a+b) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot (2+4) \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find the second integral where $x\\in [1,3],$ we compute the area ${A}_{2}$ of the quarter-circle cut out of the square as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & ={s}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}\\pi \\cdot {r}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =4-\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(3)={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=6+(4-\\pi )=10-\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da3ddabd6e1b99db68538a49fbeacfe91dd1f81d24b1020a197b6e80597ac2ba" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "10+\\pi "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "10-\\pi "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "6-\\pi "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "8+\\pi "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "8-\\pi "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/assets/3676c09e0fa21bbf0a0d1828fbb6e6095f83965ea3edd0538786ca11d2fb317e.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Given $g(t)={\\int }_{-2}^{t}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x,$ determine the value of $g(2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Evaluating $g(t)$ at $t=2,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\ng(2)={\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThis integral gives the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/assets/6dad371f36d3d5cbb88bbed40b2e3b60f94fbcad8284b0e218093c13c57d6e41.png)\n\nNote that the graph above consists of $2$ parts:\n\n- $x\\in [-2,0],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a trapezoid. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{1}.$\n\n- $x\\in [0,2],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a triangle. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\ng(2)={\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute these integrals:\n\n- To find the first integral where $x\\in [-2,0],$ we compute the area ${A}_{1}$ of the trapezoid as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot (2+3) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find the second integral where $x\\in [0,2],$ we compute the area ${A}_{2}$ of the triangle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(2) & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=5+2=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da3ddabd6e1b99db68538a49fbeacfe91dd1f81d24b1020a197b6e80597ac2ba" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/state.json" "file_sha256" "e64186c4f6d99028dc5d92ef4aab7f082fa435dfa296219d1ca4c5359c169245" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-10876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $F(\\pi)$ where $\\displaystyle F(x) = \\int_1^x \\dfrac 1 t\\,\\textrm d t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/example-10876.json" "file_sha256" "80d57b28d1dd12653b9b55554ed98c3e1faad441e5e75b8a638b0fb308d9f19d" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-10876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Evaluating $F(x)$ at $x=\\pi,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\nF\\!\\left(\\pi\\right) = \\int_{1}^{\\pi} \\dfrac{1}{t} \\, \\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nThen, computing the definite integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\pi ) & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|\\,{|}_{1}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/example-10876.json" "file_sha256" "80d57b28d1dd12653b9b55554ed98c3e1faad441e5e75b8a638b0fb308d9f19d" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-10884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The graph of a function $y = f(x)$ is shown below. Given $\\displaystyle g(t)= \\int_{-2}^{t} f(x)\\, \\textrm{d}x,$ determine the value of $g(3).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/assets/7eb2c5d91fde9279e2533ff77d86ea30e9c21c3a026d26e84e4d04293da6f63a.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/example-10884.json" "file_sha256" "2c881db5a41de7139dd80e4adb90b674ed65b410f23c65423e44b2d038a0957c" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-10884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Evaluating $g(t)$ at $t=3,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\ng(3) = \\int_{-2}^{3} f(x)\\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nThis integral gives the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/assets/8bf473cbddef213fb959112fb72ca9a13d9aae4d72c64ce5a68110f349e34d33.png)\n\nNote that the graph above consists of $2$ parts:\n\n- $x \\in [-2,0],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a trapezoid. This corresponds to the area $A_1.$\n\n- $x \\in [0,3],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is another trapezoid. This corresponds to the area $A_2.$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\ng(3) = \\int_{-2}^{3} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x = \\underbrace{\\int_{-2}^{0} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x}_{A_1} + \\underbrace{\\int_{0}^{3} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x}_{A_2}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute these integrals:\n\n- To find the first integral where $x \\in [-2,0],$ we compute the area $A_1$ of the trapezoid as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot (2+3) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find the second integral where $x \\in [0,3],$ we compute the area $A_2$ of the trapezoid as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot (2+4) \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(3) & ={\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=5+9=14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/example-10884.json" "file_sha256" "2c881db5a41de7139dd80e4adb90b674ed65b410f23c65423e44b2d038a0957c" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-10877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that a pool has a small hole and that water is leaking out at a rate of $t^{1/3}$ gallons per minute, where $t$ is the time in minutes. If at time $t = 0$ the pool contains $100$ gallons of water, how many gallons of water will remain in the pool after $t$ minutes?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/example-10877.json" "file_sha256" "639adaf90c0483255a26bda71870b0a565f2ec797461e44d9f54c7fca0627fe4" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-10877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $f(t) = -t^{1/3}$ be the rate at which the volume of water in the pool is changing, and let $F(T)$ be the amount of water in the pool after $T$ minutes. Note that $f(t)$ is negative to indicate that the volume is decreasing.\n\nUsing our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nF(T) \t\t\t= F(0) + \\int_0^T f(t)\\,\\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(T) & =F(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =100-{\\int }_{0}^{T}{t}^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =100-\\frac{3{t}^{4/3}}{4}{|}_{0}^{T} \\\\  & =100-\\frac{3(T)^{4/3}}{4}+\\frac{3(0)^{4/3}}{4} \\\\  & =100-\\frac{3}{4}{T}^{4/3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's rewrite our final answer in terms of the original variable $t.$ We have\n\n$$\nF(t) = 100 - \\dfrac {3}{4}t^{4/3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/example-10877.json" "file_sha256" "639adaf90c0483255a26bda71870b0a565f2ec797461e44d9f54c7fca0627fe4" "basis" 1148 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010573/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/assets/68786f08e73998de597d0d9eea5be3031f322785c05835cf7eccfa7837f36d7b.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. It consists of two lines and the arc of a semi-circle of radius $3.$ Given $g(t)={\\int }_{-3}^{t}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x,$ determine the value of $g(6).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b17f93243c3b4c733cf6573512f1f095b38177d272887b810f6bb0fb50db4" "basis" 1307 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Evaluating $g(t)$ at $t=6,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\ng(6)={\\int }_{-3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral gives the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/assets/b553755a624031408b8374d06c8dc8dbf33c3ddc8d372332c945bad7e42ef068.png)\n\nNote that the graph above consists of $2$ parts:\n\n- $x\\in [-3,0],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a triangle. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{1}.$\n\n- $x\\in [0,6],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a semi-circle and a rectangle below it. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\ng(6)={\\int }_{-3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute these integrals:\n\n- To find the first integral where $x\\in [-3,0],$ we compute the area ${A}_{1}$ of the triangle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find the second integral where $x\\in [0,6],$ we compute the area ${A}_{2}$ of the semi-circle and the rectangle below it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2}+bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}+6\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\pi +18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(3) & ={\\int }_{-3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=\\frac{9}{2}+(\\frac{9}{2}\\pi +18)=\\frac{45+9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b17f93243c3b4c733cf6573512f1f095b38177d272887b810f6bb0fb50db4" "basis" 1307 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3f7650d9b45cfe48131e292bb92067ed329e52f5d0481fe39a618231e77497d6" "basis" 1307 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b17f93243c3b4c733cf6573512f1f095b38177d272887b810f6bb0fb50db4" "basis" 1307 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "18+9\\pi "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b17f93243c3b4c733cf6573512f1f095b38177d272887b810f6bb0fb50db4" "basis" 1307 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "23+9\\pi "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b17f93243c3b4c733cf6573512f1f095b38177d272887b810f6bb0fb50db4" "basis" 1307 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{36+9\\pi }{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b17f93243c3b4c733cf6573512f1f095b38177d272887b810f6bb0fb50db4" "basis" 1307 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{45+18\\pi }{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b17f93243c3b4c733cf6573512f1f095b38177d272887b810f6bb0fb50db4" "basis" 1307 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{45+9\\pi }{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b17f93243c3b4c733cf6573512f1f095b38177d272887b810f6bb0fb50db4" "basis" 1307 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{45+9\\pi }{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b17f93243c3b4c733cf6573512f1f095b38177d272887b810f6bb0fb50db4" "basis" 1307 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The bacteria culture in a lab increases at a rate of ${e}^{2t}$ per hour. If, after $2$ hours, there are $2\\,000$ bacteria in the population, approximately how many bacteria are in the population after $6$ hours?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b17f93243c3b4c733cf6573512f1f095b38177d272887b810f6bb0fb50db4" "basis" 1307 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $s(t)={e}^{2t}$ be the rate at which the number of bacteria is changing and let $S(T)$ be the total number of bacteria and in the population after $T$ hours.\n\nUsing our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nS(T)=S(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{T}s(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(T) & =S(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{T}s(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\,000+{\\int }_{2}^{T}{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}{|}_{2}^{T} \\\\  & =2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2T}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2T}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the number of bacteria in the culture after $T=6$ hours, we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\nS(6)=2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2\\cdot 6}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4}=2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{12}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4}≈83\\,350.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b17f93243c3b4c733cf6573512f1f095b38177d272887b810f6bb0fb50db4" "basis" 1307 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3f7650d9b45cfe48131e292bb92067ed329e52f5d0481fe39a618231e77497d6" "basis" 1307 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b17f93243c3b4c733cf65